 ("309","FFE","Production — LED video walls (upstage + overhead)",0,1_500_000,"2","HOUSE-SETUP LOGIC PUTS THIS IN PHASE 2. Artists bring or rent their own video design, so an owned wall is the production element most likely to sit unused or be struck for a visiting rig. FT DID buy LED: $415,575 at Infinity and $231,796 at Park (both Audiotek, shared purchase) — worth knowing before repeating it. The dev budget line carries a $1,400/SF note with no quantity. What MUST go in on day one is the mounting structure and the power to feed it; the panels can follow once the calendar proves the spend."),
